## Measured descriptions (12 October 2026)

The full numbers are in `measured` of each look. Here are the values the blocks must reproduce.

- **void-black-grain.** The black is pure digital black, not a dark grey: the corner median is #000000, luma p95 is 0, and the high-pass standard deviation is 0.0. 3D and graphic shots therefore need no grain layer. In 27 % of all frames the mean luma is below 8. (12 October 2026)
- **low-key-cool-grade.** On live shots the median luma runs from 14 (S19) to 56 (S21) and p99 from 100 to 208, while the darkest 10 % of pixels sit at #000000 to #060606, so the blacks are crushed. Mid tones are shifted blue (mean B minus R from +4 in S14 to +17 in S22) and turn violet in S19 (#100c1f) and S22 (#211b41). The corners are 0.78 as bright as the centre at 22.9 s (a vignette). Grain high-pass std is 0.31 to 0.36. (12 October 2026)
- **depth-of-field-blur.** On a 3x3 sharpness map (variance of the Laplacian, normalised), live shots have one sharp cell (1.0) and every other cell below 0.05. S03 is sharp in a vertical band in the centre column (0.5 to 1.0), with sides below 0.24. S12 is sharp at top left and in the centre and soft in the right column (0.016). (12 October 2026)
- **screen-ui-emission.** Blue tiles ramp #031d69, #042cb1, #0b70bd, #bac7da; the violet screen ramps #221f72, #3d4ab2, #919bd5, #cdd4e9; skin lit by the screen has a median of #4c3737. UI content (text, numbers, icons) is never copied. Only the gradients and the light spill are looks. (12 October 2026)
- **copper-metal-rim.** The body ramps #1f0603, #331005, #4f2114, #96492f, #dc9174 (p5 to p95), and a lit rim ramps #a63d21, #f1a563, #f5bc7c, #fcd9a8. Highlights stay warm and never reach pure white. (12 October 2026)
- **bloom-halo.** Measured as mean luma by distance from the saturated core, in bins of 0-2, 2-4, 4-8, 8-16, 16-32, 32-64 and 64-128 px at 1080p: chip 249, 211, 200, 190, 173, 133, 76; ring 243, 171, 143, 109, 81, 58, 42; orb rim 210, 156, 138, 117, 98, 83, 62. Around the green beam the halo is saturated, from #0b7c07 at 2 px down to #042d03 at 128 px. These long tails call for a sum of about three gaussians (radius near 3, 15 and 60 px). (12 October 2026)
- **text-card-fade.**
