## Notes and limits (12 October 2026)

- **What a look excludes.** Hands, people, fabric, circuit boards and device geometry are live footage or 3D models, not shader looks. Only their grade, light and blur are listed here. The device body itself belongs to the existing `templates/device3d` path. (12 October 2026)
- **Soft shadows.** No distinct soft shadow was found: devices float on pure black, and the final shots show a reflection rather than a shadow, so no shadow look is listed. (12 October 2026)
- **Not separated as its own measure.** The colour of the centre droplet of the orb and the arch was not measured separately; its size is already fitted by `archglow.py` (`dot_y`, `dot_r`). (12 October 2026)
- **Screen time versus effort.** Priority follows screen time, as asked. The first look, the black void, costs one flat colour, so the real effort order would rather be: grade, depth of field and bloom first, then copper, strata, arch glow and smoke. (12 October 2026)
